      "message": "\u003e But does that really fully prevent the race? What if the host\u0027s and pKVM\u0027s created_vcpus are also incremented in the meantime by another thread on another CPU, right after the host allocates the vmexit trace buffer but before pKVM handles the dump_vmexit_trace hypercall using this buffer? Then we have the same race?\n\nYou are right, this race can still happen and this patch will not fix the issue. I will drop this patch.\n\n\u003e Yes, without propagating the error code to the host, the already dumped vmexit data can still be printed.\n\nMakes sense. So I shall have the fix very simple by unlocking the spinlock before returning and not worry about propagating the error.",
